Default DOWNLOAD_TOML_LIB to OFF so iceoryx_posh consumes the vendored cpptoml.

The inline cpptoml ExternalProject download+build runs host git/doxygen that
fail under the VxWorks SDK (they load a VxWorks libc.so.1 off LD_LIBRARY_PATH).
cpptoml_vendor installs cpptoml + its cmake config; with DOWNLOAD_TOML_LIB=OFF
iceoryx_posh resolves it via find_package(cpptoml), avoiding the inline build.
--- a/iceoryx_posh/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/iceoryx_posh/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 find_package(Threads REQUIRED)
 find_package(iceoryx_hoofs REQUIRED)
 
-option(DOWNLOAD_TOML_LIB "Download cpptoml via the CMake ExternalProject module" ON)
+option(DOWNLOAD_TOML_LIB "Download cpptoml via the CMake ExternalProject module" OFF)
 option(TOML_CONFIG "TOML support for RouDi with dynamic configuration" ON)
 option(ONE_TO_MANY_ONLY "Restricts communication to 1:n pattern" OFF)
 
